# ♿ ACCESSIBILITY RULES - PROTECTED ASSET

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: NEVER DELETE OR MODIFY WITHOUT EXPLICIT PERMISSION

### 🎯 ACCESSIBILITY STANDARDS
- **WCAG 2.1**: AA compliance minimum
- **Screen Reader**: Full compatibility required
- **Keyboard Navigation**: Complete keyboard access
- **Color Contrast**: Minimum 4.5:1 ratio

### 🔍 SCREEN READER COMPATIBILITY

#### **Semantic HTML**
- **Headings**: Use proper heading hierarchy (h1 → h2 → h3)
- **Landmarks**: Use semantic elements (nav, main, section, article)
- **Lists**: Use proper list elements (ul, ol, dl)
- **Forms**: Use proper form labels and fieldset

#### **Alt Text Requirements**
- **Images**: Descriptive alt text for all images
- **Decorative Images**: Use `alt=""` for purely decorative images
- **Complex Images**: Provide detailed descriptions
- **Charts/Graphs**: Include data summary in alt text

### ⌨️ KEYBOARD NAVIGATION

#### **Focus Management**
- **Visible Focus**: Clear focus indicators on all interactive elements
- **Tab Order**: Logical tab sequence through page
- **Skip Links**: Provide skip navigation for main content
- **Focus Trapping**: Proper focus management in modals

#### **Interactive Elements**
- **Buttons**: All buttons must be keyboard accessible
- **Links**: All links must be keyboard accessible
- **Forms**: All form controls must be keyboard accessible
- **Custom Components**: Ensure keyboard support

### 🎨 VISUAL ACCESSIBILITY

#### **Color and Contrast**
- **Text Contrast**: Minimum 4.5:1 for normal text
- **Large Text**: Minimum 3:1 for large text (18px+)
- **Color Independence**: Don't rely solely on color for information
- **Focus Indicators**: High contrast focus indicators

#### **Typography**
- **Font Size**: Minimum 16px for body text
- **Line Height**: Minimum 1.5 for body text
- **Font Choice**: Use readable, sans-serif fonts
- **Spacing**: Adequate spacing between lines and paragraphs

### 📱 RESPONSIVE ACCESSIBILITY

#### **Mobile Considerations**
- **Touch Targets**: Minimum 44x44px for touch targets
- **Viewport**: Proper viewport meta tags
- **Zoom**: Allow zoom up to 200%
- **Orientation**: Support both portrait and landscape

#### **Responsive Design**
- **Breakpoints**: Test accessibility at all breakpoints
- **Content**: Ensure content is accessible on all screen sizes
- **Navigation**: Mobile navigation must be accessible
- **Forms**: Mobile forms must be usable

### 🧪 TESTING REQUIREMENTS

#### **Automated Testing**
- **Lighthouse**: Run accessibility audits
- **axe-core**: Use axe testing library
- **ESLint**: Enable accessibility linting rules
- **Continuous**: Test accessibility in CI/CD

#### **Manual Testing**
- **Screen Reader**: Test with NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver
- **Keyboard**: Complete keyboard navigation testing
- **Color Blindness**: Test with color blindness simulators
- **Mobile**: Test on various mobile devices

### 🚨 PROTECTION STATUS
- **NEVER DELETE** this file
- **NEVER MODIFY** accessibility standards without approval
- **REQUIRES EXPLICIT PERMISSION** for any changes
- **ALWAYS REFERENCE** this file for accessibility decisions

### 📋 IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLES

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Follows accessibility rules
<button 
  className="px-4 py-2 bg-forest text-white rounded"
  aria-label="Submit form"
  onClick={handleSubmit}
>
  Submit
</button>

<img 
  src="/hero-image.jpg" 
  alt="Professional team collaborating on communication strategy"
  className="w-full h-auto"
/>

